top to bottom direction
title Redis Recovery - Global Target Structure\nNew classes and all connections: Pending implementation
class "Browser EventReducer\nPer Chat / connection generation" as UI
package "Mate public boundary (Pending implementation)" {
  class "ChatStreamController\nSingleton / VO boundary" as MC
  class "ChatObservationService\nSingleton" as MS
  class "AuthorizedPublicProjector\nSingleton / immutable caller context" as MP
  class "ClawObservationClient\nSingleton / protected internal API" as Client
  class "PublicHistoryRepository\nStable event identity mapping" as MH
}
package "Claw application and core" {
  class "SessionObservationController\nPending implementation / VO" as CC
  class "SessionObservationService\nPending implementation / singleton" as CS
  class "ObservationSubscription\nPending implementation / per connection\ncursor + bounded buffer" as Sub
  class "RuntimeEventProjector\nExisting extension point\nPer execution" as Runtime
  class "ExecutionPreviewAccumulator\nPending implementation / per execution" as Acc
  class "HotEventPublisher\nPending implementation / singleton" as Pub
  class "CommittedEventCatchUpService\nPending implementation / singleton" as Repair
  interface "HotEventStore\nPending implementation" as Store
  class "RedisHotEventStore\nPending implementation / singleton" as Adapter
  class "RuntimeSessionRepository\nExisting; incremental read extension pending" as Repo
}
database "Redis primary\nSnapshot + bounded Stream\nPending implementation" as Redis
database "GaussDB\nAuthoritative events and execution state" as DB
UI --> MC : authorized read / reconnect
MC --> MS : request VO
MS --> Client : private Session mapping
MS --> MP : project snapshot and events
MP --> MH : resolve stable public IDs
Client -down-> CC : independent read-only SSE
CC --> CS : authorized observation
CS "1" *-- "0..*" Sub : owns readers
Sub --> Store : snapshot at C; read after C
CS --> Repair : reconcile committed records
Runtime "1" *-- "1" Acc : accumulates before HTTP queue
Runtime --> Repo : commit complete events
Acc --> Pub : immutable preview batch
Runtime --> Pub : after database commit
Repair --> Repo : bounded committed-event read
Repair --> Pub : idempotent full-event repair
Pub --> Store : publish / checkpoint
Adapter ..|> Store
Adapter --> Redis : scripts + XREAD
Repo --> DB : short transactions
MH --> DB : public projection ownership
note bottom of Runtime
Existing database control polling is retained.
Disconnect does not cancel execution.
Redis does not restore a failed Java execution.
end note
note bottom of Store
Immutable DTOs only; no raw credentials.
New API models are proposed, not yet integrated.
Snapshot + cursor share one atomic read boundary.
end note
@enduml

