title Reopen One Browser View - Pending implementation
participant Browser
participant "Mate reader" as Mate
participant "Claw reader" as Reader
database Redis
participant "Claw executor" as Exec
database "Authoritative history" as DB
Exec -> Redis : Atomically publish preview snapshot and cursor
Browser -> Mate : Reopen authorized Chat stream
Mate -> Reader : Map Chat; open independent internal read stream
Reader -> Redis : Read snapshot and cursor C atomically
Redis --> Reader : Preview and cursor C
Reader --> Mate : Initial snapshot
Mate --> Browser : Replace incomplete previews
Exec -> Redis : Append batch after C
Reader -> Redis : Read batches after C
Redis --> Reader : Ordered incremental batch
Reader --> Mate : Normalized update
Mate --> Browser : Public preview update
Browser -> Mate : Read complete history
Mate -> DB : Authorized public history projection
DB --> Mate : Complete events
Mate --> Browser : Reconcile; completed events win
note over Reader,Exec
  Reader disconnect never cancels the executor.
  Completion commits to DB before preview removal.
  Redis failure uses history fallback, not a zero-loss guarantee.
end note
@enduml
